            <ArticleTitle>An unusual problem during surgical removal of a broken guidewire.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>829-30</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>At operation, it proved impossible using traction alone to remove an angioplasty guidewire that was lodged in an intermediate artery. The problem was solved by passing a Teflon catheter over the wire, thus protecting the left main coronary artery while freeing the entrapped distal end of the guidewire.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
